{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/234104-crafting-purview-drawing-inspiration","id":234104,"title":"Crafting purview: drawing inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-19T06:13:03-07:00","id":234104,"title":"Crafting purview: drawing inspiration","content":"1e scion was awesome but i always felt it was missing something in terms of equipment. You had your relics you used for your powers and that was pretty much it till you reach godhood. which is unfortunate considering the many varied items of power in myths. Heck most of the relics used by mythological gods has awesome origin stories of how they were forged, from being made of meteoric iron to being forged by dwarves. It would be cool to see a crafting or artifice purview. To this end i'd actually draw on similar rules to Mage's main three magic item rules: the enchanted item, the imbued item and the artifact, to use as a baseline for how divinely crafted items functioned.<br /> <br /> Enchanted items in mage make a normal item better, more durable, sharper and giving a bonus to it's use. For the artifice purview this would be what heroes could make, a better stronger version of a normal item. say a scion wanted to remake Mjolnir and had crafting; at this level he'd make a hammer that would be difficult to break and could dent a truck. For balance reasons i'd just give a flat bonus rather than one that scaled with skill or power otherwise you'd have characters with pen knives that could decapitate a dragon (unless that's okay with you)<br /> <br /> Imbued items in mage gave a power to an item and a supply of mana to power it. For the artifice purview they could create items like this when they become a demigod, i'd allow them to incorporate a single purview power or other ability to the item, Either letting it power itself or allowing the sign to power it with their legend. for instance the previous scion, now a demigod reforges his hammer to now shoot forth a lightning bolt at his enemies. partially to avoid abuse and partially to add to them thematically i'd put in requirements for their crafting materials, such as needing dragon's hide for a coat making you immune to fire, nymphs blood for lipstick that charms those kissed or wood from a tree in the underworld for a staff that let's you control ghosts.<br /> <br /> Artifacts in mage were items of power that couldn't be crafted but instead came from a higher realm, they always had their own power and usually their own stories. For the artifice purview these could only be forged by gods and could be used to increase power over an entire purview, awakening scion's potential and perhaps having unique abilities of their own. Going back to our example scion who has attained godhood he can now forge mjolnir itself (this is just an example i doubt thor would like having two of those around) he could now craft a hammer that gives a bonus to the storm purview, calls up gales when wielded, and strikes with the force of ten. the balance of items like these would probably be rooted in whatever rules were used for godhood so i won't try to guess at them here.<br /> <br /> It can be difficult to balance items of power so that they aren't either making the characters able to stack bonuses to a ridiculous extreme or just spam the powers till they're blinging more than a D&amp;D character. This could be handled in alot of ways such as the aforementioned requirement for crafting materials but to avoid spamming you might want to consider a penalty for creating them like temporarily investing a point of legend that doesn't return for, say, a month or so. other options would be having a maximum number of each type of artifact, although while that may prevent them from from mass producing artifacts it would seriously hamper what they could do (you never saw Hephaestus asking Zeus if he could dismantle his lightning bolt so he could make a new toy)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}